    "Undergraduate (English Track) < Undergraduate < Admissions >  Welcome to Kyungsung University(*)\n스킵네비게이션\n본문바로가기\n주메뉴바로가기\nKYUNGSUNG UNIVERSITY\nUndergraduate (English Track)\n메인으로 이동\nAdmissions\nAbout Kyungsung\nAdmissions\nAcademics\nCampus Life\nMember Service\nMy Page\nEtc\nUndergraduate\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nUndergraduate (English Track)\nUndergraduate (English Track)\nUndergraduate (Korean Track)\nNotice\nApply Link\nScholarship\nAdmissions\nAdmissions\nUndergraduate\nUndergraduate (English Track)\nUndergraduate (Korean Track)\nNotice\nApply Link\nScholarship\nGraduate\nAbout Admissions (for Graduate)\nNotice (for Graduate)\nSNS 공유하기\n페이스북\n블로그\n트위터\n북마크\n인쇄\nUndergraduate (English Track)\nUndergraduate (Korean Track)\nNotice\nApply Link\nScholarship\n2026 Fall Semester Admission Guideline (Download)\nAvailable Majors for English Track Undergraduate Program\nSchool/Department\nSchool of Global Studies\nMajor\nGlobal Business Administration\nSchool/Department\nSchool of Global Studies\nMajor\nGlobal Hospitality Management\nSchool/Department\nSchool of Global Studies\nMajor\nGlobal Korean Studies\nSchool/Department\nSchool of Global Engineering Studies\nMajor\nGlobal Mechanical Design Engineering\nSchool/Department\nSchool of Global Engineering Studies\nMajor\nGlobal IT Engineering\nEligibility Criteria\n❍ A prospective international applicant\n(1) must be a non-Korean,\n(2) must either hold or be expected to hold a high school diploma or a certificate of high school equivalency\n(3) must have obtained IELTS score of at least 5.5 (or) at least iBT TOEFL score of 71.\n※ Exception: English native speaking countries such as USA, Canada, Australia, and etc.\n❍ For a prospective transfer international student\n(1)2nd Year Transfer\na) Completed(or is expected to complete) a year(2 semesters) and earned required credit for completion at a domestic or overseas university\nb) Received(or is expected to receive) a degree in a domestic or overseas 2~3 year community college\n(2) 3rd Year Transfer\na) Completed(or is expected to complete) 2 years(4 semesters) and earned required credit for completion at a domestic or overseas university\nb) Received(or is expected to receive) a degree in a domestic or overseas 2~3 year community college\nScholarship for English Track Undergraduate Program\nFirst Semester(based on English Proficiency Score)\nStatus\nType\nStudent\nScholarship\n(Tuition Fee Waiver)\nCriteria\nRemarks\nFirst-year\nand\nTransfer\nTuition\nFee\nWaiver\nKorean\nand\nEnglish\nTracks\n100%\n(Special Selected Scholar)\n- A special selected scholar by overseas sister university based on the MOU/agreement\n- A special selected scholar by Yayasan Kyungsung Indonesia based on his/her qualified academic performance during the language training period (selects within 10% of Yayasan Kyungsung Indonesia from the number of student admission)\n- A special selected scholar based on the highest score of the admission evaluation process among a holder of at least Test of Proficiency in Korean (TOPIK) level 5 for Korean Track admission, a holder of at least TOEFL iBT 79 or at least IELTS 6.0 or holds the nationality of a country that uses English as its mother tongue or uses English as a legal official language for English Track admission\nAmong a special selected scholar\nwho qualifies for one of the three criteria shall be finally chosen,\nand a limited number of\napplicant(s) per semester\nshall be finally chosen\nbased on the current\nset budget.\n※ If there is no qualified\nstudent, no one is finally\nselected\nEnglish\nTrack\n50%\nA holder of at least TOEFL iBT 104 or at least IELTS 7.5\nwaiver’ section\n40%\nA holder of at least TOEFL iBT 95 or at least IELTS 7.0\n30%\n- A holder of at least TOEFL iBT 71 or at least\nIELTS 5.5 - A student of English-speaking foreign nationality\nAdmission\nFee\nWaiver\nFirst-Year\nStudents\nExemption of\nAdmission Fee\n- National Institute for International Education (NIIED) Global Korea Scholarship (GKS) Scholars\n- A special selected scholar selected by a sister university\nAfter the First Semester\nStatus\nType\nStudent\nScholarship\n(Tuition Fee Waiver)\nPrevious Grade of Average (GPA)\nOther Qualified Students\nEnrolled\nForeign\nStudents\nTuition Fee Waiver\nKorean\nand\nEnglish\nTracks\n100%\nAverage rating of 3.5 or higher for the previous\nsemester\nSpecial Selected Scholar\n90%\nTop 1.5%\n80%\nTop 3%\n70%\nTop 5%\n60%\nTop 7%\n50%\nTop 10%\n40%\nTop 20%\n30%\nTop 30%\n20%\nTop 100%\ninter\nnational\nstudent\ncouncil\nmember\n30%\nA representative of the international student association by country\n20%\nVice representative of the international student association by country\nApplication Procedure\nApplication Procedure\n1\nOnline Application\nLink : Go to the site\n2\nRead Admission Guide\n3\nFill in Application Form\n4\nInterview\n5\nAnnouncement of Final Successful Candidates\n6\nIssue Payment Invoice\n7\nPayment of School Fees\n8\nVisa Process\n9\nStudent Registration\n10\nArrival to Korea / Orientation\nPoint of Contact\nPerson in Charge\n(Mr.) Changkeun Koo\nEmail\nMain : admissions@ks.ac.kr  (sub) feelso333@ks.ac.kr\nInternational\n+82-(0)51-663-4064\nFax\n+82-(0)51-663-4069\nAddress\nThe Genesis Bldg. 30 #201-2, 309 Suyeong-ro Namgu, Daeyeon Dong, Busan, Republic of Korea 48434"
